  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Three skating stations",
  "description": "Split the group into three teams, each starting at its own station, and rotate after 6–8 minutes: station 1 to 2, 2 to 3 and 3 to 1.\n\nStation 1 – crossovers: the players skate round the centre circle with crossovers, forwards and then backwards. On the signal everyone changes direction. Last lap with a ball. Station 2 – start and stop: a relay with two teams. The player sprints to the cone, stops sharply, sprints back and tags the next one. Station 3 – forwards, stop, backwards: a relay where the player skates forwards to the cone, stops and skates backwards back. Make the distance longer each round.\n\nA coach at each station counts and encourages. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Crossovers: edge your skates, turn your upper body in towards the circle and push off with the inside leg."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Start: short, quick strides at first and stick in one hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Stop: rise a little, bend your knees and turn your skates across against the ice."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Backwards: low position, sit down and keep your head up."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
